/-! # A kernel-feasible packed Seventh source tensor

The packed tensor of the Seventh axis (worker `gforest`, `seventhSrcVecW w`) is the triality image
`twTriTen w 2048 (srcSeventhYX w) (srcSeventhYL w).sh.odd`, whose kernel evaluation (a word action and
a long sum of single entries) is memory-heavy.  `seventhSXF w` stores the numerators (over
`8192`) as compact literal columns with `16`-bit fields, re-spaced to width `w` by `respace`;
one cross-sum kernel check at width `104` binds it to the source tensor (`seventhSXF104_ten`), and
`seventhSXF_bnd` gives its tensor bound at every width `w ≥ 16`. -/

@[expose] public section
